    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "SFT",
      "narration_text": "We start with a machine that writes restaurant reviews. Good ones, bad ones, it does not care — it just writes. So first we show it two hundred nice reviews, and ask it to write more like those.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidReviewBot",
          "props": {
            "before": "-0.06",
            "after": "+0.57",
            "sample": "the dessert was really delicious and the room was excellent ."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.6,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.84,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidReviewBot",
        "at": "2026-10-19T23:28:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "LIMIT",
      "narration_text": "That helps, and it is also as far as showing examples can take you. To go further the machine needs to know not just what good looks like, but which of two things is better. And for that, somebody has to say.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE NEXT PROBLEM",
            "headline": "Examples only get you so far.",
            "kicker": "now it needs to compare, not copy"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.2,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.99,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-19T23:28:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "NOISY",
      "narration_text": "So we show people pairs of reviews and ask which is nicer. 1500 times. But here is the thing nobody mentions: people are not perfect at this.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidNoisyLabels",
          "props": {
            "agreePct": "77.3%",
            "agreeN": 0.773
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.4,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.37,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidNoisyLabels",
        "at": "2026-10-19T23:28:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "JUDGE",
      "narration_text": "Now we train a judge. It reads thousands of those pairs and learns to give any review a score, trying to agree with what people picked. It ends up a little better than the people were — but it learned from their mistakes too.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "BUILDING THE JUDGE",
            "headline": "A judge built from imperfect opinions.",
            "kicker": "it is a copy of a slightly blurry original"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.9,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.82,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-19T23:28:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "BLINDSPOT",
      "narration_text": "And when you test that judge carefully, you find the gaps. On ordinary reviews it does fine — great beats terrible, exactly as you would hope. But look at the highlighted rows. Add the word not, and it barely notices. Say the same nice thing three times over, and it likes you more, not less.",
